ritualistic behavior** — hoarding, repetitive movements; (5) **Hyperorality and dietary changes** — craving sweets, binge eating, attempting to eat inedible objects; (6) **Neuropsychological profile** showing **executive dysfunction with relative sparing of memory and visuospatial function**. Brain MRI shows **frontal and/or anterior temporal** atrophy, often asymmetric. FTD typically has an earlier onset (45-65 years) compared to AD (>65). Treatment is supportive: SSRIs for disinhibition and compulsive behaviors, trazodone for agitation. (Ref: Hazzard''''s Ch. 72; Rascovsky Criteria 2011)'),
