* → higher risk of **Dementia with Lewy Bodies**; (3) **Language impairment** → may progress to **Primary Progressive Aphasia** (FTD spectrum). This contrasts with **amnestic MCI**, which most commonly progresses to **Alzheimer''''s disease**. Not all MCI patients progress — some remain stable and ~15-20% may even revert to normal cognition. (Ref: Petersen MCI Criteria; Hazzard''''s Ch. 72)'),
