 considered normal) and **all functional abilities are fully preserved**. This contrasts with: **MCI** — objective impairment on cognitive testing (typically MoCA 18-25) with preserved functional independence; **Dementia** — objective cognitive impairment PLUS functional dependence (cannot manage ADLs or IADLs independently). Reassurance and education are appropriate; no pharmacotherapy is indicated. (Ref: AGS Geriatrics At Your Fingertips; Hazzard''''s Ch. 72)'),
